en:
It indicates the presence of two successive urban junctions close together (a short distance apart) (it has a white background).

At the first junction turning left is prohibited (because of the 'NO ENTRY' sign) and you turn right for Via Gemona;

at the second junction (at the end) you turn right for the city centre and for Trieste (Grado and Cividale), while you turn left for the hospital or for Austria (Tarvisio and Tolmezzo).
